Local integration changes:
- Embedded leandvb_main entry point, no X11 GUI, telemetry via src/leansdr_monitor.hh.
- Bounded LDPC process pool via src/ldpc_pool.cc. Ordered asynchronous results,
  explicit batch lengths, partial pipe I/O, finite-input draining and child reaping.
- Scheduler keeps running while asynchronous FEC work is outstanding.
- --ldpc-batch accepts 1..32; --nhelpers is a global 1..8 worker limit.
- RS/BCH result and detected PLS callbacks into the local monitor.
- Publish PLS telemetry only after the selected DVB-S2 MODCOD/frame-size mask
  accepts a frame, keeping the fixed GUI mode stable across corrupted headers.
- Fix fd_const >= 0 check; explicit return for invalid decoder standard.
- Add --help alias and document embedded options, helper framing and worker limits.
- Byte-table BCH polynomial remainders for 14/16-bit DVB-S2 polynomials,
  replacing bitwise division without changing syndromes or error correction.
  Generic polynomial widths retain the original division path.

Acquisition patch by Ondrej OK1CDJ, reported in upstream issue #41:
https://github.com/pabr/leansdr/issues/41
https://github.com/ok1cdj/ESP32-DATV-RX/blob/esp32-atv/tools/leandvb-acquisition.patch
- Full-length normal-frame PLHEADER search.
- Initial PLSCODE frequency/phase fit across allowed candidates.
- Reject initial locks with implausible PLHEADER MER.
The patch's vector include was added manually; its other five hunks applied.
The known upstream QPSK 4/5 short-frame carrier ambiguity is not claimed fixed.

Additional LDPC table transcription corrections checked against the independent
xdsopl DVB-S2 tables, with regression checks for all 21 tables:
- B.2 normal 1/3: move 32910 and 40870 to their preceding rows (degree 12).
- C.3 short 2/5: last 12 rows have degree 3, not 12.
- C.7 short 3/4: first row has degree 12, not 3.
These also correct the test transmitter; decoding tests use the independent
xdsopl helper so shared transmitter/receiver table errors cannot silently pass.
